Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Connect pymalloc block transitions to retained lifetime authority
Upstream: CPython 3.13.7
Upstream-Archive: https://www.python.org/ftp/python/3.13.7/Python-3.13.7.tgz
Upstream-SHA256: 6c9d80839cfa20024f34d9a6dd31ae2a9cd97ff5e980e969209746037a5153b2
Build-Variants: native port, Capstone domain
Depends-On: cpython-3.13.7-0002-capability-provenance.patch
Apply-From: upstream source root, with patch --batch --forward --fuzz=0 -p1

Use scalar arena cursors and capability-backed pool/block accessors. Preserve
pymalloc's choice of size classes, lazy carving, free-list order, pool caching
and arena retention. Reissue authority on successful realloc, including in-place
resize; copy only the old requested payload. Raw fallback uses a separately
accounted allocator with the same lifetime hooks. Native hooks are transparent.

